 `tern-exchange --config-dir PATH --state-dir PATH` is an **internal** bounded, one-shot UTF-8 JSON stdin/stdout bridge to the private same-UID control socket, not a public agent API or daemon startup command. Exchange v1 carries `version:1`, `kind:"tern"`, window identity, positive safe-integer `epoch`/`sequence`, bound `instance_id` after registration, `agents` and at most one `results` receipt. Replies have `ok`, `instance_id`, `generation`, optional `command:{operation_id,pane,text}`, `error`, and optional failure `error_code` exactly `binding_required|instance_changed|source_retired|receipt_rejected|rejected`. The first unbound snapshot is result-free and its reply is command-null. A lost first registration reply recovers by new window identity on the normal next poll; `source_retired` resets without ask replay. An exactly bound `receipt_rejected` drops only reports captured in that request. Window-scoped `pane` is identity; labels are metadata. States `idle|working|waiting_input|exited` do not establish completion; `accepted|failed` describes the one previously offered ask, not model completion. Separate bounds are **256 KiB request JSON** and **512 KiB complete encoded reply including LF**. Actual serialization determines admission before pending/offer state, with definite TooLarge rejection, not guessed Herdr headroom. Unknown/duplicate fields, stale identities and foreign receipts fail closed. Offers are once-only with no PTY/shell fallback or unknown-delivery retry. The shared Herdr+Tern source budget is 64: only expired offline Tern sources can be reclaimed after pending work is finalized; never live/Herdr sources, and IDs never repeat. The control accept loop's existing 100 ms monotonic tick expires freshness at **>=5 seconds**, independently of serial Herdr polling/client I/O. New epochs create new generations. Same-UID trust is local, not remote Tern authentication.
 
 `status.herdr_socket` reports the immutable configured UpdateContext path even in Tern-only mode, not an active endpoint; no fake registration/socket is required. Endpoint identity rejects empty/relative paths, accepts equal absolute paths even with missing socket/parent, otherwise compares full canonical aliases or canonical parents plus the same filename, never basename alone. The plugin persists canonical `connection={version=1,executable,config_dir,state_dir}` in one KV commit after whole-object validation and before profile/incarnation switch. Cancel/failure retains the old connection. Three legacy keys are adopted once only when canonical data is absent, then cleaned after commit; malformed canonical data never falls back. External shared-profile commits fence delayed callbacks.
 
+Current-source `status` includes `observation_mode:"auto"|"herdr"|"tern"` and typed `host_connections:{herdr:NUMBER,tern:NUMBER}`. Counts represent connected, coherent, currently supported provider sources, not installation, configured paths, enabled switches or session counts; `data_connected` is true when either provider count is nonzero. Observation scope can hide session rows without inventing or erasing provider connection evidence. A host change retires disabled-source generations and route/observation epochs: late snapshots cannot revive them, stale exact session keys fail, and queued/offered prompts are never replayed or rerouted to another provider after switching back.
+
+The native and Tern plugin defaults use the same config/state profile: `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/herdr/plugins/config/desktop-pet` and `${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/herdr/plugins/desktop-pet`. Existing isolated profiles are retained, never automatically merged, overwritten or deleted. To explicitly choose an existing base profile, copy the actual executable/config/state triple from native **Connection → Connection settings** into Tern's **Configure desktop pet connection**, then Connect. The plugin validates all three and commits once before switching identity; cancellation/save failure keeps the old route and delayed callbacks cannot cross the cutover. Native `HERDR_PLUGIN_CONFIG_DIR`/`HERDR_PLUGIN_STATE_DIR` take precedence over CLI paths; clear or align inherited injected paths for explicit manual profile commands.
