+**Auto observes actual Herdr and Tern connections simultaneously**, not fallback or priority selection. Installing either host/plugin does not make it connected. Each provider shows its own **Connected / Waiting / Disabled** status from actual connections; session sources remain distinct even when titles or paths match. New profiles default to Auto. Existing preferences without a saved host retain Herdr; existing saved choices are preserved. Source startup precedence is explicit `--host auto|herdr|tern`, then explicit `HERDR_PET_OBSERVATION_MODE`, then saved `observation.host`, then Auto for a new profile. Legacy `both` is accepted only as a migration input and saved/reported as `auto`.
